btop on IBM AIX
===============

This package installs the AIX port of btop, a resource monitor for the
terminal (https://github.com/aristocratos/btop).

Requirements
------------
* AIX 6.1 TL7 or later: one package for 6.1, 7.1, 7.2 and 7.3 (started on
  6100-07, 6100-09, 7100-02, 7100-05, 7200-05 and 7300-04). The binary is built
  against the AIX 6.1 libraries and probes the libperfstat structure size at
  run time, so newer libperfstat versions are read correctly.
* rpm.rte 4.9.1.3 or newer (AIX Toolbox for Linux Applications). Hosts with
  the old rpm.rte 3.0.5 cannot install the package (it needs
  rpmlib(PayloadFilesHavePrefix)): unpack the tar archive of the same release,
  see below. The RPM refuses to install over a /usr/bin/btop that is not its
  own symlink.
* bos.perf.libperfstat (part of the base operating system).
* No UTF-8 locale is needed. The launcher /opt/btop/bin/btop adds --force-utf
  when none is active, and sets TERM=xterm-256color when TERM is empty.

Install, start, remove
----------------------
    rpm -ivh btop-<version>-<release>.aix6.1.ppc.rpm   # "aix6.1" names the minimum release; rpm on 7.1-7.3 accepts it
    btop                      # /usr/bin/btop -> /opt/btop/bin/btop
    rpm -e btop

Tar archive (rpm.rte 3.0.5). It contains
only opt/btop, so nothing outside that directory is touched:

    cd / && gzip -dc btop-<version>-<release>.aix6.1.ppc.tar.gz | tar -xf -
    ln -s /opt/btop/bin/btop /usr/bin/btop     # optional
    rm -rf /opt/btop /usr/bin/btop             # uninstall

Without root, unpack into any directory and start the launcher there; it
follows symlinks and runs the btop.bin next to it:

    mkdir ~/btop && cd ~/btop && gzip -dc /path/to/btop-<version>-<release>.aix6.1.ppc.tar.gz | tar -xf -
    ~/btop/opt/btop/bin/btop

A 256-colour terminal (xterm-256color, PuTTY with "xterm-256color") gives
the intended look; aixterm and vt100 work with the "tty" theme or
`btop --low-color`.

Layout
------
    /opt/btop/bin/btop             launcher (shell script)
    /opt/btop/bin/btop.bin         the program (64-bit XCOFF, static C++ runtime)
    /opt/btop/share/btop/themes    themes shipped with btop
    /opt/btop/share/doc/btop       README.md, LICENSE, this file
    /usr/bin/btop                  symlink to the launcher (RPM; optional with the tar)
    ~/.config/btop                 per user configuration
    ~/.local/state/btop.log        per user log

What the port shows
-------------------
CPU, load and frequency from libperfstat (DLPAR changes are followed), memory
and paging space, mounted file systems from mntctl/statvfs plus the physical
volumes (hdiskN) with their I/O, network interfaces, and processes from
getprocs64 (kernel "wait" processes are hidden). Per file system I/O needs
LVM statistics (`lvmstat -e -v <vg>`). Not available on AIX: sensors,
battery, GPU. Inside a WPAR the header shows "WPAR".

Provenance
----------
Built on an AIX 7.2 host with IBM Open XL C/C++ 17.1.3 against an AIX 6.1
sysroot and a statically linked libc++ 19.1.7 (the C library functions AIX 6.1
lacks, aligned_alloc and the POSIX 2008 locale calls, are replaced inside that
runtime). Source: branch aix-public of the fork https://github.com/mawelo/btop;
the patch series, the upstream base commit and the signed release files are
in https://github.com/mawelo/aix-btop. `btop --version` prints the
commit the binary was built from.
